[rotated_bc] WARNING: rotated free slip on ['Lower', 'Upper'] takes a given normal that varies along the wall, and the normal velocity is fixed on the whole boundary. The constant-pressure continuity row then holds a weighted sum of the wall slip fixed (the weights are where the given normal differs from the facet-weighted normal; the mean pressure is its multiplier), a constraint the continuous problem does not have. Where the wall facets are unequal it can stop the velocity converging, on manufactured free-slip solutions (#1168): 63 to 67 % error on an elliptical annulus, and 32 to 34 % on an annulus whose wall nodes have slid along the circles, neither falling with refinement. Annulus and SphericalShell walls as built have equal facets and are not affected; the error appears once wall nodes slide along the wall (a mesh mover with slip, adaptation, a free surface). Use normal=None (the default, facet-weighted normal) unless the given normal is needed for an exact rigid-rotation null mode.
